<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2290/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2290/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/L22/current/TOOL2290/>;
    dc:modified '2026-04-20T11:13:19'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SEAL AA500'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'SEAL Analytical AutoAnalyser 5500'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A fully automated Segmented Flow Analysis (SFA) system, ideal for water and seawater analysis. It comprises a modular system which integrates an autosampler, peristaltic pump, chemistry manifold and detector. The sample and reagents are pumped continuously through the chemistry manifold, and air bubbles are introduced at regular intervals forming reaction segments which are mixed using glass coils. This is an upgrade of the AA3(HR), offering a full start-up to shut-down automation, a smaller footprint, and a simplified workflow. The instrument uses a high resolution dual beam LED digital photometer with optional LED wavelength modules 250 - 880 nm and optional 10 - 50 mm flow cells.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:L22::TOOL2290'^^xsd:string .
